flowchart TB
    accTitle: The trust boundaries of Paperless Sync
    accDescr: Seven numbered arrows cross a trust boundary. 1: the browser of an administrator sends requests to Paperless Sync in Nextcloud. 2: the app calls Paperless-ngx. 3: the app writes the files below the base folder of the target user. 4: whoever may write to the inbox folder puts files there. 5: a workflow of Paperless-ngx, or anyone on the network, calls the webhook of the app. 6: a member of the group that may send files sends files of their own from Files. 7: a rule of Flow, which only an administrator saves, sends the files that it matches, of any user. The app keeps the API token and the hash of the secret of the webhook in the credentials manager. The browser, the writers of the inbox, Paperless-ngx, the callers of the webhook, the senders in Files and the users whose files a rule of Flow matches are untrusted and have a dashed red border.

    credentials[("Credentials<br>manager:<br>API token,<br>hash of the<br>webhook secret")]
    browser(["Browser of an<br>administrator"])
    callers(["A workflow of<br>Paperless, or anyone<br>on the network"])
    app["Paperless Sync<br>in Nextcloud"]
    writers(["Whoever may<br>write to the<br>inbox folder"])
    senders(["A member of the<br>group that may<br>send files, in Files"])
    flow(["Whoever writes a file<br>that a rule of Flow<br>matches"])
    paperless[("Paperless-ngx")]
    files[("Files below<br>the base folder<br>of the target user")]

    credentials --- app
    browser -- "1" --> app
    callers -- "5" --> app
    senders -- "6" --> app
    flow -- "7" --> app
    app -- "2" --> paperless
    app -- "3" --> files
    writers -- "4" --> files

    classDef untrusted fill:#c9302c1f,stroke:#c9302c,stroke-width:2px,stroke-dasharray:4 3
    class browser,callers,writers,senders,flow,paperless untrusted
